WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.577
A nested loop means one loop runs inside another.

00:00:03.577 --> 00:00:06.152
The outer loop controls rows.

00:00:06.152 --> 00:00:10.382
For each row, the inner loop goes through three columns.

00:00:10.382 --> 00:00:14.064
That creates six row-column combinations in total.

00:00:14.548 --> 00:00:21.085
Nested loops are useful for grids, pairwise combinations, and some matrix-style tasks.

00:00:21.085 --> 00:00:27.591
But readability drops quickly when too many loops are nested, so keep the structure as simple as possible.
